<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baol</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baol was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolof">Wolof</a> kingdom in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> that was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> state within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jolof-empire">Jolof Empire</a>. After Jolof's defeat at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-danki">Battle of Danki</a> around 1549, Baol, along with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cayor">Cayor</a> and others, became independent. It remained a separate kingdom until French colonial rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baol.jpg" alt="Baol" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HetmanTheResearcher · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Baol_Map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
